# Everything here is sent to the Docker daemon as build context, and `COPY . .` puts it in the image.
# Without this file the context carries the local .venv (about 800 MB) and the model files (another
# few hundred MB), which makes every build slow and the image needlessly large.

# Local Python environment, never used inside the image (the image installs its own).
.venv/
venv/

# Model files are mounted read-only by docker-compose.yml, not baked in.
models/

# Local settings: docker compose passes them at run time through env_file, so they must not be in the image.
.env

# Repository and tooling.
.git/
.github/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.part

# Host-side launchers and deployment files; the container is started by compose or systemd.
run_local.ps1
start_esm_service.cmd
deploy/

# Tests need requirements-dev.txt, which the image does not install. `--verify` and the API are what runs
# in the container; the tests run where the repository is checked out.
tests/
pytest.ini

# Documentation.
*.md
LICENSE
